Hello folks,

I just discovered mibbit.com through a person on #lojban and I must say, that I 
like it.
It's basically like CGI:IRC, but looks much better. It's implemented in 
javascript (AJAX sa'e) and works in many browsers (unless, of course, javascript 
is turned off for security reasons).

What's your opinion on putting a mibbit "applett" onto lojban.org?
We could either drop it into an IFrame, link to it (new tab/new window) or link 
to mibbit.com and have the server address and channel name pre-filled.

I think mibbit is much more appealing than CGI:IRC is (and it has tab completion 
for nicks! and an integrated pastebin!) :)
   - Timo


